<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Dhanyawadi</h1><p class="st-meta">100 CE – 370 CE (approx.) · capital Dhanyawadi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first kingdom of Arakan in the Rakhine chronicles, remembered as the home of the Mahamuni image, the most revered Buddha statue in Myanmar.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Rakhine chronicles place the founding of Dhanyawadi far back in antiquity, with a line of kings ruling from a walled city in the Kaladan valley. Historians date the excavated city, with its brick walls and palace site, to the early centuries CE, and the register's 1st to 4th century span follows the later chronicle chronology.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Dhanyawadi was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>-growing and trading kingdom on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a>, open to Indian influence. Its fame rests on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahamuni-buddha">Mahamuni Buddha</a>, which tradition says was cast in the Buddha's lifetime under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandrasuriya">Chandrasuriya</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> inscriptions and coins of the following Chandra kings show Indian-style kingship.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>According to the chronicles, power shifted south to the new city of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-waithali">Waithali</a> around 370. The Mahamuni image remained at Dhanyawadi until 1784, when the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/konbaung-dynasty">Konbaung dynasty</a> carried it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amarapura">Amarapura</a>; its temple, now within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandalay">Mandalay</a>, is still a major pilgrimage site.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 100 CE – 370 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mainland Southeast Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:61.69%;width:5.37%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>100 CE – 370 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dhanyawadi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Chandrasuriya</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism, Hinduism</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dhanyawadi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=235&amp;focus=kingdom-of-dhanyawadi" aria-label="Kingdom of Dhanyawadi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7189 1416 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Dhanyawadi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7509 1672L7509 1672"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7509 1672h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7509 1672h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7509 1672h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dhanyawadi. <a href="/atlas?year=235&amp;focus=kingdom-of-dhanyawadi">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
